<form class="dataset-search" method="get" action="{{ ds_action }}" data-server-search>
{#
		The data scope the screen is showing travels with the search. Without it the request arrives
		with no scope at all, the server falls back to its default, and the scope control resets the
		moment anybody types - which is what happened when the inline Administration form was
		replaced by this shared control and its hidden field was left behind. The page number is
		deliberately absent: a new search returns to page one.

		Nothing here names a scope that the reader has not been shown, because this comment reaches
		the rendered page and an ordinary reader must never learn that a second population exists.

		The isset guard is deliberate. A caller that never sets the key at all leaves an undefined
		variable, and strict_variables turns that into an error for the entire page rather than an
		empty value - which is how the Account routes began failing when they first used this
		control. Callers
		should still supply the key; this makes forgetting it a missing hidden field rather than a
		broken page.
	#}
	<div class="field">
		<label for="{{ ds_name }}-search">{{ ds_label }}</label>
		<input type="search" id="{{ ds_name }}-search" name="{{ ds_name }}_q" value="{{ ds_value }}" placeholder="Type to search" autocomplete="off" maxlength="120"
		       hx-get="{{ ds_action }}"
		       hx-trigger="input changed delay:300ms, search"
		       hx-target="#{{ ds_name }}-region"
		       hx-select="#{{ ds_name }}-results"
		       hx-swap="innerHTML"
		       hx-include="closest form"
		       hx-sync="this:replace"
		       hx-indicator="closest .dataset-search">
	</div>
	<div class="dataset-search-actions">
		<span class="dataset-search-status" aria-live="polite" role="status">Searching…</span>
		<noscript>
			<button class="btn btn-soft btn-sm dataset-search-submit" type="submit">Search</button>
		</noscript>
		{% if ds_value %}
			<a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="{{ ds_action }}">Clear</a>
		{% endif %}
	</div>
	<p class="help">
		Searches every matching record, not only the rows on this page.
	</p>
</form>
